From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <rainb@tfwno.gf>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 06:10:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] driver: Build with GCC

- MmProbeAndLockPages() raises on a bad user buffer. GCC has no
  try/except, so probe in a helper that uses the ReactOS PSEH macros
  there and keeps try/except for MSVC.
- Spell the security descriptor's alignment DECLSPEC_ALIGN(8), which the
  WDK and GCC headers both map to their compiler's syntax.
- Link the send NBL with if/else: the two arms of the ?: are pointers of
  different types, which GCC rejects.
- Cast the out-pointers of ObReferenceObjectByHandle() to VOID **, the
  thread routine to KSTART_ROUTINE * and the process to PRKPROCESS.
- Forward-declare TunDispatchPnp under its own name.
---
 driver/wintun.c | 64 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 43 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/wintun.c b/driver/wintun.c
index 5adf230..1993f0a 100644
--- a/driver/wintun.c
+++ b/driver/wintun.c
@@ -9,6 +9,9 @@
 #include <ndis.h>
 #include <ntstrsafe.h>
 #include "undocumented.h"
